7. Local inference tier — engine binary and base model checkpoint
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The optional local model tier that `aif configure` sets up (with your
  consent) runs two third-party artifacts. Neither is compiled into the `aif`
  binary: the inference engine is distributed as its own archive, and the
  model checkpoint is downloaded at configure time and verified by sha256
  digest. On the product surface both present under de-branded names
  (`aif-server`, `aif-model-base-v1`); this section is the binding upstream
  attribution for both, and the upstream names appear here — the legal home —
  by design.

  Component:   llama.cpp (`llama-server`), distributed as `aif-server`
  License:     MIT License  (third_party/MIT.txt)
  Copyright:   Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors

  The `aif-server` inference engine binary is the `llama-server` program from
  the llama.cpp project (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), built
  unmodified from the source commit pinned in the AIF source tree
  (runtime/daemon/scripts/zaya_toolchain.lock) and renamed only at the
  packaging step. The MIT copyright and permission notice is retained here,
  in third_party/MIT.txt, and as LICENSE.llama.cpp.txt inside the engine
  archive itself; each engine build's exact source commit is recorded in the
  build_info.txt shipped next to the binary.

  Component:   ZAYA1-8B (base checkpoint), served as `aif-model-base-v1`
  License:     Apache License, Version 2.0  (third_party/Apache-2.0.txt)
  Copyright:   Copyright Zyphra and the ZAYA1 model authors

  The model artifact the configure flow downloads and serves as
  `aif-model-base-v1` is `ZAYA1-8B-Q4_K_M.gguf`
  (sha256 330ad2b15a6dabc9d955e7f10f4f7ee220180f06ee3bee4d06062218966f2c74),
  a GGUF quantization of Zyphra's ZAYA1-8B model
  (https://huggingface.co/Zyphra/ZAYA1-8B, Apache-2.0), obtained from the
  Apache-2.0-licensed GGUF packaging at
  https://huggingface.co/Abiray/ZAYA1-8B-GGUF at the revision pinned in the
  vendored launcher. It is the PUBLIC BASE checkpoint — NOT the finetuned
  firewall model. The digest above is the identity the runtime's integrity
  gate verifies; `aif doctor` reports the running model by its de-branded
  label and this digest.

